        "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $3$ | $8$ | $3$ | $-2$ |\n|  | $\u2193$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $2$ |\n|  | $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}=3{x}^{2}+2x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{x}^{2}+2x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{|}_{0}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}-x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{0}^{2}+{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}-x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{3}-{0}^{3}]+[{2}^{2}-{0}^{2}]-[2-0] \\\\  & =8+4-2 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
